        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the lack of proper locking mechanisms (specifically, the absence of a read lock) when looking up transactions, which led to inconsistencies in the handling of records during operations like adding, updating, and deleting. This oversight resulted in missing records after the compaction process, as the controls for read and write locks were broken.

